with a few million particles.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:44.270
We can, of course, scale up the simulation,
and then, we are back at seconds per frame

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:47.449
land, but it is still blazing fast.

00:05:47.449 --> 00:05:54.280
If you look here, we can go up to 27 times
faster, so in one all-nighter simulation,

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.750
I can simulate what I could simulate in nearly
a month.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.180
Sign me up!

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.680
